@prefix orexis: <http://example.org/orexis#> .
@prefix execution: <http://example.org/orexis/execution#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix sh:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix : <http://example.org/orexis/execution#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<> a orexis:OntologyGraph .    # this document is one graph, and this is what it is

#  OREXIS EXECUTION.
#  THE EXECUTION PACKAGE'S OWN WORDS: an intention, its steps and acts, the window a step is good
#  in, how an action is carried out — and nothing the executor does not read or write. A term
#  returns with the thing that reads it and not before (a-term-nobody-reads-is-annotation).

execution:IntentionGraph a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf orexis:Graph ; rdfs:label "Intention graph" ;
    rdfs:comment "What the agent is DOING: commitments adopted, standing and resolved, kept in the belief base's volume as a graph of the agent's own, not public, so a restart finds them and planning reads what is walked by this kind." .

execution:CommittedStepGraph a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf orexis:BeliefGraph ; rdfs:label "Committed step graph" ;
    rdfs:comment "ONE STEP AN INTENTION HAS COMMITTED TO, as a belief holding over its landing window: from the step's `execution:notBefore` to its `execution:notAfter` plus the patience (knowledge/domain/execution/committed-step.md). Written by the executor at adoption, one graph per step, carrying the step's filling as the plan states it and the window's two lengths in seconds; closed at the instant the world answers the step or the intention ends, and forgotten once it has ended. A belief and not a reading: no plan forks it, nothing holds the world to it, and a drift reads it at an instant — the dose a bed is committed to is a flow its soil's prediction accumulates, so a later want is searched against a future that contains the earlier plan, and the start and end of the window are happenings of every prediction (a-prediction-accumulates-rates-between-happenings)." .

execution:landsWithinS a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain execution:Step ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
    rdfs:label "lands within seconds" ;
    rdfs:comment "On a committed step: how long after its opening the step's change lands at the earliest — `execution:landsAt` less `execution:notBefore`, in seconds of the one timeline. Stated as a number beside the two instants because the engine binds nothing for the stretch between two instants (no cast of a duration to a number binds, measured), so a drift dividing a rise by this window could not compute it from the plan's instants." .

execution:answeredWithinS a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain execution:Step ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
    rdfs:label "answered within seconds" ;
    rdfs:comment "On a committed step: how long after its opening the world must have answered the step at the latest — `execution:notAfter` less `execution:notBefore` plus the patience, in seconds; the window closes then, and an intention whose step is unanswered by then fails. The low trajectory of a drift reading a committed step assumes this, the latest landing, which is how a late landing widens the corridor." .

execution:adopts a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain execution:Intention ;
    rdfs:label "adopts" ;
    rdfs:comment "The plan an intention commits to — an orexis:PlanGraph planning published and owns — referred to and never copied: the plan's steps are read where planning wrote them, and the intention holds only its own rows." .

execution:keptBelow a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain execution:Step ; rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:label "kept below" ;
    rdfs:comment "Said by planning of a step whose predicted fact a rule the store holds concludes: not the executor's to take fictively. When it falls due the executor waits for the want that keeps it one level down (execution:keptBy) and takes it by waiting on that want." .

execution:keptBy a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain execution:Step ;
    rdfs:label "kept by" ;
    rdfs:comment "The want that keeps a step one level down, written by planning beside the want it mints when the step falls due; the executor records it on the step's act (execution:refinedBy) and waits on it, and planning withdraws the want once nothing stands at the step." .

execution:Intention a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "Intention" ;
    rdfs:comment """One commitment: one plan for one want, adopted at a moment, standing at a step, resolved at another moment or still standing. The lifecycle is two timestamps and an outcome, not a state machine: standing is `adoptedAt` without `resolvedAt`, and how it ended is `outcome` (knowledge/domain/execution/intention.md).""" .


execution:pursues a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "pursues" ;
    rdfs:comment "The want an intention — or a plan handed down, on its root — was found for. A want an intention walks is neither searched nor handed a second plan until the intention resolves, or a trigger of soft commitment reopens it — a want a constraint couples to it arriving, or a belief arriving that makes a world of its plan impossible (knowledge/domain/execution/commitment.md)." .

execution:by a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain execution:Intention ; rdfs:range execution:Step ;
    rdfs:label "by" ;
    rdfs:comment "The step this intention stands at now. Moved along `execution:then` when the world answers what the step predicted; absent once the intention resolves." .

execution:endsAfter a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain execution:Intention ; rdfs:range execution:Step ;
    rdfs:label "ends after" ;
    rdfs:comment "The step in flight this intention ends after: written by the executor when planning has reconsidered the want the intention pursues and replaced its untaken steps with a joint plan (knowledge/domain/execution/commitment.md, #905). The step is held to its prediction as any taken step is — never cancelled, the hard grain of commitment — and when the world answers it the intention resolves `superseded` rather than moving on; where the patience runs out on it first, it resolves `failed` as ever." .

execution:Step a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "Step" ;
    rdfs:comment "One orexis:Action filled in and PLANNED — not yet done: the action it fills and a triple per parameter, when it may be taken (execution:notBefore), the earliest and the latest its change lands (execution:landsAt, execution:notAfter), what the search predicted taking it changes, as two graphs it names (execution:adds, execution:retracts), and what follows (execution:then). A plan is steps; an intention commits to them (execution:step) and stands at one (execution:by)." .

execution:Act a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "Act" ;
    rdfs:comment "The RECORD that a step was taken: which step (execution:of), when (execution:takenAt), whether anyone took it (execution:taken) — history, and only history. Written by the executor as the step leaves flight. A step kept one level down carries `execution:refinedBy` the want it became." .

execution:of a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain execution:Act ; rdfs:range execution:Step ;
    rdfs:label "of" .

execution:takenAt a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain execution:Act ; rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:label "taken at" ;
    rdfs:comment "When the executor handed the step to its taker — the record, against the step's `execution:notBefore`, which is the requirement." .

execution:Command a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf execution:Operation ;
    rdfs:label "Command" ;
    rdfs:comment "An operation sending a device a command: an `sh:select` run over the present beliefs when the step is taken, with the step's parameters as `$tokens`, `$me` and `$now`, answering `?actuator` and `?payload`, the JSON document the device is sent. How much to pour or how long to heat is sized here from the situation as it is, never by the search, and the container sends each answer through the transport that reaches the actuator." .

execution:Saying a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf execution:Operation ;
    rdfs:label "Saying" ;
    rdfs:comment "An operation telling a peer something: an `sh:construct` run over the present beliefs when the step is taken, with the step's parameters as `$tokens`, `$me` and `$now`, whose result is one or more DOCUMENTS. A graph is an IRI the result says is `execution:to` an agent; what the result says of that IRI and what hangs off it through blank nodes is the graph's content, but for its kind (an `rdf:type` the vocabulary puts beneath `orexis:Graph`), its period (`dcterms:temporal`) and the agents it is to, which are the rows about it. The agent believes what it said, and the container sends each document to each agent it is to through the transport; several sayings of one order are merged by graph." .

execution:Fictive a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf execution:Operation ;
    rdfs:label "Fictive" ;
    rdfs:comment "An operation writing the step's own prediction into the agent's readings: the implementation of an action whose effect is its own physics, where no instrument reports what taking it did — a hanoi move, a courier's drive — so the present answers because nothing else could have. An executor built `fictive` takes every step so, the shorthand for a world that exists only in the store." .

execution:to a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:range orexis:Agent ;
    rdfs:label "to" ;
    rdfs:comment "Whom a document a saying is for — written in the result of an `execution:Saying`, read by the container to address it, and never part of the document itself." .

execution:doneAt a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain execution:Act ; rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:label "done at" ;
    rdfs:comment "When the taker returned, taken or not. With `execution:takenAt` it is how long the taking took, in the one timeline; it is NOT when the step's change landed in the world, which is the world's to say through a reading and is held against the step's `execution:landsAt`, the prediction, by whoever holds the world to the step." .

execution:taken a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain execution:Act ; rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:label "taken" ;
    rdfs:comment "Whether the step was taken; false is an attempt the taker could not carry out, and the intention fails with it." .




execution:notBefore a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain execution:Step ; rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:label "not before" ;
    rdfs:comment "The window's opening — a REQUIREMENT on the step and never a record of it. Written by the plan's extraction as the instant of the world the step is taken in, so a plan placed at its root's instant carries that placing across; the executor's timekeeper hands a step to the queue no earlier. What actually happened is the act's: `execution:takenAt` and `execution:doneAt`." .


execution:adoptedAt a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain execution:Intention ; rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:label "adopted at" .

execution:resolvedAt a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain execution:Intention ; rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:label "resolved at" ;
    rdfs:comment "Absent while the intention stands. Its absence IS the standing state — no flag to keep in step." .

execution:outcome a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain execution:Intention ; rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:label "outcome" ;
    rdfs:comment "How it ended: `done`, `failed`, `abandoned` (the intention a step of it was kept below for ended undone), or `superseded` (a second plan for the want, past the patience; or a joint plan that replaced its untaken steps, after its step in flight — `execution:endsAfter`)." .

execution:step a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain execution:Intention ; rdfs:range execution:Step ;
    rdfs:label "step" ;
    rdfs:comment "Every step of the plan this intention commits to. `execution:by` names the one it stands at now; `execution:then` orders the rest." .

execution:then a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain execution:Step ; rdfs:range execution:Step ;
    rdfs:label "then" ;
    rdfs:comment "The step that follows this one in the plan committed to (#510). Written when the plan is extracted; the executor moves `execution:by` along it when the world answers a step, taking the next with no search." .

execution:landsAt a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain execution:Step ; rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:label "lands at" ;
    rdfs:comment "The EARLIEST the step's change can show: the start of the period of the world the step reaches — the step's instant plus the least the action says its landing takes — shifted by how late the step was taken. The executor holds the world to the step from this instant on; before it, the world says nothing of the step." .

execution:notAfter a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain execution:Step ; rdfs:range xsd:dateTime ;
    rdfs:label "not after" ;
    rdfs:comment "The LATEST the step's change can show: the end of the period of the world the step reaches — the most the action says its landing takes, summed along the plan — shifted as `landsAt` is. A patience past it with no answer, the step is unmet and its intention fails; the two agree where the action's landing is exact (#596). The window a committed step is believed over closes a patience past it." .

execution:partOf a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain execution:Step ; rdfs:range execution:Step ; rdfs:label "part of" ;
    rdfs:comment "The plan a step belongs to — written by the extraction, read by the executor to adopt the plan's steps." .


#  WHAT A STEP PREDICTS, as two graphs it names — stated, and never asserted: a world where the
#  dose has landed is not this world (a-steps-prediction-is-two-graphs-it-names). The kinds are
#  beneath orexis:Graph alone, so no reader of the present, the public knowledge or a package's
#  scratch is handed one; a reader reaches them through the step, by `execution:adds` and
#  `execution:retracts`. The engine computes the effect's diff when a world is forked or the plan is extracted, compares the
#  present to it when the step is held to the world, and writes a fictive step from it. They
#  were one JSON literal of canonical triples, which nothing could query, abbreviate or compare
#  in a pattern (#759).

execution:AddsGraph a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf orexis:Graph ; rdfs:label "Adds graph" ;
    rdfs:comment "The facts a step predicts its world GAINS: every triple its action's effect added to the world it was applied to, as the terms they are — and nothing a prediction moved between the world the step is taken in and the one it lands in, which is no act of the agent's (#919). One graph per step, named by the step's `execution:adds`, written by the plan's extraction beside the step and copied with the plan; the executor holds the world to it — the step is answered once the present holds every one of them — and a fictive step writes them into the state. In an imaginarium, also one per possible world forked in a later ground than its parent's, derived from that world (`prov:wasDerivedFrom`), which the extraction copies. Not a belief and not public: what it says is what WOULD hold, and no reader asking for the present is handed it." .

execution:RetractsGraph a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf orexis:Graph ; rdfs:label "Retracts graph" ;
    rdfs:comment "The facts a step predicts its world LOSES: every triple its action's effect took away from the world it was applied to. The other half of the prediction, a graph of its own because a graph is classified per kind it holds and a retraction is a different claim from an addition; named by the step's `execution:retracts`, and the step is answered only while the present holds none of them." .

execution:adds a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain execution:Step ; rdfs:range execution:AddsGraph ;
    rdfs:label "adds" ;
    rdfs:comment "The graph of facts this step predicts the world gains. One declaration: the effect the search planned on is the effect the world is held to. A step naming neither this nor `execution:retracts` predicts nothing and moves as soon as it is taken; one naming an empty graph is answered the moment it lands." .

execution:retracts a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain execution:Step ; rdfs:range execution:RetractsGraph ;
    rdfs:label "retracts" ;
    rdfs:comment "The graph of facts this step predicts the world loses — the reading that stood before the dose, the peg the disk was on. The present must hold none of them for the step to be answered." .
execution:patienceS a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain orexis:Agent ; rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
    rdfs:label "patience seconds" ;
    rdfs:comment "How long a standing intention blocks re-adoption of the same one. Within it, a second plan for the same want is absorbed; past it, the new one supersedes the old. Also how long past its latest landing (`execution:notAfter`) a step may go unanswered before its intention fails. The executor's default stands until an agent states its own." .

#################  How an action is carried out — execution's  #################

execution:implementation
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain orexis:Action ;
    rdfs:range execution:Implementation ;
    rdfs:label "implementation" ;
    rdfs:comment "How an action is carried out when a step filling it is taken — what actually goes out, sized from the present. The search never reads it: it plans on the effect, and the world is held to the effect whichever operations carried it out." .


execution:Implementation
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Implementation" ;
    rdfs:comment "An action's operations, `execution:operation` to each, grouped by `sh:order` as an effect's rules are: every operation of one order is made from the same present, and a later order's from the present after what the earlier ones said was believed and revised." .


execution:operation
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:domain execution:Implementation ;
    rdfs:range execution:Operation ;
    rdfs:label "operation" .


execution:Operation
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Operation" ;
    rdfs:comment "One thing taking a step does: a command to a device, a document to a peer, or writing the effect itself for a world with nothing to report it. The kinds are execution's (`execution:Command`, `execution:Saying`, `execution:Fictive`)." .

execution:refinedBy a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain execution:Act ;
    rdfs:label "refined by" ;
    rdfs:comment "The want an act kept its step one level down as — written when the container's `refine` answered one instead of the step being taken. The step then waits on that want and not on the clock: while an intention walking it stands, patience does not run; when one ends undone, the step fails at once; and when the step's own intention ends undone, whatever walks that want is abandoned with it." .
